{#
    Twelve months of spend, drawn from the forecast.

    The design's chart plotted income against expenses. A subscription tracker
    has no income, so this is what it does have: each renewal in the month it
    actually falls, with scheduled price changes and trial conversions applied
    from their own dates. It is the same call the Forecast page makes, so the
    two screens cannot disagree about a month.

    Two lines, where there used to be bars: the upper one is that figure, the
    lower one is the same months with the trials taken out, and the band
    between them is what converting trials will add. A trial is the only future
    cost still worth a decision, and one line either hid it or overstated what
    is being paid today.

    The chart itself is `partials/spend_chart.twig`, which the analytics
    screen's spending trajectory also renders — one payload, one picture, drawn
    in two places.
#}
{% import 'partials/spend_chart.twig' as trend %}

<section class="card chart-card">
    <header class="card-header">
        <h2>{{ t('dashboard.spend_chart') }}</h2>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="/forecast">{{ t('nav.forecast') }}</a>
    </header>

    {#
        Said under the heading rather than in it: "Forecast, next 12 months"
        names the window, and what it leaves out is that these are projected
        figures and which currency they are stated in. Only when there is a
        picture to describe — an unconvertible chart says why it is not drawn
        instead, and a currency line above that message would be claiming a
        total the card has just refused to state.
    #}
    {% if chart.is_drawable %}
        <p class="muted">{{ t('dashboard.spend_chart_note', {'currency': chart.currency}) }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {{ trend.spend_chart(
        chart,
        'dashboard-spend-data',
        chart.has_trials
            ? t('dashboard.spend_chart_alt', {'currency': chart.currency})
            : t('dashboard.spend_chart_alt_single', {'currency': chart.currency}),
        t('dashboard.part_month_note'),
        t('dashboard.chart_unconvertible', {
            'currencies': chart.unconvertible|join(', '),
            'currency': chart.currency,
        })
    ) }}
</section>
